## `examples/s3-2017/` — RTU/SCADA Logic

### 🟡 Moderate Issues

#### 9. SCADA Reads From Its Own Address, Not RTU2A ([scada.py L39](file:///c:/Users/harsh/Desktop/icps_project/examples/swat-s1/../s3-2017/scada.py#L39))

```python
# co_00_2a = self.receive(CO_0_2a, RTU2A_ADDR)   ← intended
co_00_2a = self.receive(CO_0_2a, SCADA_ADDR)      ← reads own loopback
```

SCADA is reading coil data from **itself** instead of from RTU2A. This appears to be a leftover debugging line — the real receive is commented out.

**Recommendation**: Uncomment the `RTU2A_ADDR` line and remove or guard the `SCADA_ADDR` loopback.

---

#### 10. RTU2B `else: pass` Is a Silent Error ([rtu2b.py L84–86](file:///c:/Users/harsh/Desktop/icps_project/examples/swat-s1/../s3-2017/rtu2b.py#L84-L86))

```python
else:
    pass
    # print("ERROR")
```

When `count > 11` (which happens when `len(wadi2_list)/3` is larger than 12), no registers are sent and the error is silently swallowed.

**Recommendation**: At minimum log an error; ideally raise an exception or reset `count/offset`.

